{ON CAM}
ONTARIO IS SPENDING 1-POINT-2 BILLION DOLLARS TO BUILD 12 NEW LONG-TERM CARE HOMES.

{VO}
THE PLAN ANNOUNCED TODAY ADDS ABOUT 24-HUNDRED BEDS... MOSTLY IN THE G-T-A AND OTTAWA.
THE N-D-P SAYS THE PLAN FALLS SHORT.

{SOT}
[00:02:15 -- 00:02:24 | PREMIER DOUG FORD]
"EVERY SINGLE ONE OF THESE BEDS IS A SENIOR WHO GETS OUT OF A HOSPITAL HALLWAY AND INTO A PROPER HOME."

{VO}
THE N-D-P CALLS IT ANOTHER PHOTO OP... WHILE 47-THOUSAND SENIORS WAIT.
